On the topic of "culturally neutral, logical datekeeping," is there a
generally recommended lojban calendar system? How about
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Fixed_Calendar,
http://calendars.wikia.com/wiki/World_Season_Calendar or
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symmetry454 ? Logical and foreign to all seems
like a way to avoid strong cultural bias.

Asimov's World Season Calendar seems to distance itself most from the 7-day
week.

